WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.640
- [Instructor] We're told that a train

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:05.390
traveling through Japan has 90 passengers.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:09.800
52 passengers get off in Tokyo.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.800
In Kobe, another 29
passengers get off the train.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.570
No new passengers get on the train.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.820
And then they ask us how many passengers

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.200
are still on the train?

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.240
Pause this video and see if
you can work through that

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.020
before we work on this together.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.780
All right, now let's do this together.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.310
So first, what we can think about

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:33.540
is how many total passengers there are,

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:36.430
and then to figure out how many are left,

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:38.080
well, you have to start with your total,

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.380
take away 52 that get off in Tokyo,

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:43.200
then take away another
29 that get off in Kobe,

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.260
and then however many you have left,

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.030
that's how many are still on the train.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:49.670
And we can imagine that
with a tape diagram.

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.180
So let's say that the length of this tape

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.210
or the length of this rectangle

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:58.050
represents the initial,
the starting 90 passengers.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.883
So that's 90 passengers.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.750
And then how many get off in Tokyo, 52,

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.810
and I'm doing this so
that we can visualize it,

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.540
so we can think about what it looks like.

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:14.603
So we'll take away 52, which
might be something like this.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:20.323
So 52 off in Tokyo,

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:22.423
Tokyo,

00:01:22.423 --> 00:01:24.530
and then we have another 29 passengers

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:27.400
that get off the train in Kobe.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.810
So then another 29, maybe
that's something like this,

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:36.810
get off in Kobe, so 29 off in Kobe.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.100
And so how many passengers are still left?

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.610
Well, if you start with 90,

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:47.450
52 get off in Tokyo, 29 get off in Kobe,

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:51.420
then this last part of
the length of the tape,

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.010
that would be how many are left.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:57.880
So right over there,
this is the, how many,

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:02.880
how many, how many left,

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:06.080
would be the length of
this red part of the tape.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:10.270
'Cause we've taken off the
52 and the 29 off of the 90.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:12.640
So to figure that out, we
could first try to figure out

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:15.930
what is 90 minus 52?

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.100
If you haven't figured that out,

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.180
you could pause the video
and try to figure that out.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.590
All right, well, one
way to think about it,

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:26.590
90 minus 52 is the same thing
as 90 minus 50 minus two.

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:32.400
So I could write it this
way, minus 50 minus two.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.780
And you might recognize that 90 minus 50,

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:38.870
that's 9 tens minus 5 tens,
that's going to be 4 tens.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:40.370
This is going to be 40.

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:43.780
So this is going to be 40 minus 2,

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:47.970
and then 2 less than 40,
well, that's going to be 38.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:50.793
So this is going to be equal to 38.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:54.300
So if you only had that one
stop after that first stop,

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.600
you have 38 passengers left on the train.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:00.660
And so that 38 is this
amount right over here.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:03.790
But then we know another
29 get off in Kobe.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:05.750
So we need to start with that 38,

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:09.980
and 29 are going to get off, so minus 29.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:13.540
And we can view this as,
maybe we could rewrite this,

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:18.420
this is equal to 30 plus 8, that's 38,

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.430
and we're going to subtract 20 and 9.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:24.860
So subtract 20 and subtract 9.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:26.640
This wouldn't be subtract
20 and then add 9.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:27.510
That wouldn't be 29.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:30.770
We're subtracting 2 tens and 9 ones.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:32.630
So we're subtracting 20 and 9.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.800
So first, we could view
this as 30 minus 20,

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.400
which is going to be 10.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:43.993
And then we're going to
add 8 and then subtract 9,

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:46.630
subtract 9.

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:48.620
Now, what is 10 plus 8?

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.950
10 plus 8 we know is 18.

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:55.340
Now, if we subtract 9 from 18,

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:57.270
you might already know
that that's going to be 9.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.180
Another way to think about it

00:03:58.180 --> 00:03:59.690
is if you subtract 8 from 18,

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:01.150
you're going to be just left with 10,

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:02.440
and then you have one more to take away.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:04.610
So you're going to be left with 9.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:08.880
So we are going to have 9
passengers left on the train.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:12.420
Start with 90, 52 get
off, there's 38 left.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:14.170
Then another 29 get off.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.623
Now we have 9 left.

